# 4. Component boundaries

## 4.1 `ai-provider-gateway`

### Responsibility

Translate ALKEM's provider-independent AI contracts into vendor-specific protocols and normalize responses back into ALKEM contracts.

### Contains

- request/response entities;
- provider interfaces;
- provider capabilities;
- adapters;
- provider-specific translation;
- normalized errors;
- usage metadata.

### Must NOT contain

- RAG;
- vector databases;
- conversation memory;
- agent loops;
- prompt templates;
- business workflows;
- model-routing policies;
- application-specific retry/fallback strategies.

This package should be independently reusable.

---

# 5. Provider Gateway — target design

The existing implementation is the starting point.

Current concepts to retain:

- Ports & Adapters / Hexagonal Architecture;
- `CompletionRequest`;
- `CompletionResult`;
- `Message`;
- provider-specific adapters;
- async APIs;
- vendor-neutral application code.

## 5.1 Split provider capabilities

Do not require one provider interface to implement every AI capability.

Target conceptual contracts:

```text
ChatProvider
    complete(request)
    stream(request)

EmbeddingProvider
    embed(request)

CostEstimator
    estimate_cost(request)
```

An adapter may implement one or several capabilities.

Example:

```text
OpenAIAdapter
    ChatProvider
    EmbeddingProvider
    CostEstimator

AnthropicAdapter
    ChatProvider
    CostEstimator

OllamaAdapter
    ChatProvider
    EmbeddingProvider
```

Exact Python protocol organization will be decided during implementation.

## 5.2 Normalize streaming

Consumers must never parse provider-specific SSE or JSON.

Target contract:

```text
AsyncIterator[StreamEvent]
```

Initial event model may contain:

```text
TextDelta
UsageUpdate
Completed
```

MVP may start with only normalized text deltas if introducing event types adds unnecessary complexity.

## 5.3 Embedding request/result

Do not hardcode embedding models inside adapters.

Introduce explicit request data:

```text
EmbeddingRequest
    model
    inputs
```

and a provider-independent result:

```text
EmbeddingResult
    embeddings
    model
    provider
    usage?
```

## 5.4 Errors

Provider-specific HTTP errors must eventually become normalized domain errors.

Initial categories:

```text
AuthenticationError
RateLimitError
ModelUnavailableError
InvalidRequestError
ProviderConnectionError
ProviderResponseError
```

Do not implement a complex hierarchy until real adapter behavior requires it.

## 5.5 HTTP lifecycle

Avoid coupling application semantics to `httpx`.

Adapters may internally share/inject an async HTTP client to improve:

- testability;
- connection pooling;
- resource lifecycle management.

This is an implementation concern, not part of the public domain contract.

