# 10. Memory

Memory is distinct from raw chat history.

Future levels:

## Session memory

Information required during one active conversation/session.

## Persistent memory

Information reusable across sessions.

## Longitudinal memory

Information whose value comes from observing changes or continuity over time.

Examples:

- evolving project decisions;
- recurring user preferences;
- historical states;
- changes in goals;
- previous architectural choices.

Longitudinal memory is a later milestone and must not block the initial product.

