# 16. Roadmap

## Milestone 0 — Repository baseline

Goal: make the existing gateway trustworthy.

Tasks:

- run current tests;
- confirm package layout;
- clean project metadata;
- establish formatting/linting/type-checking strategy;
- establish CI;
- document architecture decisions.

Deliverable:

```text
ai-provider-gateway v0.1 baseline
```

---

## Milestone 1 — Provider Gateway v0.2

Goal: establish stable provider-independent contracts.

Tasks:

1. audit current interfaces;
2. separate chat and embedding capabilities;
3. normalize streaming output;
4. make embedding model explicit;
5. verify cost units/calculation;
6. improve adapter tests;
7. test request/response translation without real network;
8. define minimal normalized provider errors;
9. retain OpenAI, Anthropic and Ollama adapters.

Acceptance criteria:

- application code can use ChatProvider without knowing vendor;
- embedding support is optional;
- streaming consumers receive normalized output;
- adapter behavior is unit-testable without network access;
- swapping providers requires no business-logic changes.

---

## Milestone 2 — ALKEM Core

Goal: create the first orchestration layer.

Implement:

```text
AIEngine
ProviderRegistry
Model configuration
Basic explicit provider selection
```

Acceptance example:

```text
engine.generate(
    model="...",
    messages=[...]
)
```

without client code constructing vendor adapters itself.

No automatic routing yet.

---

## Milestone 3 — Developer CLI

Goal: create a usable vertical slice.

Example:

```bash
alkem ask "Explain dependency inversion"

alkem ask --provider ollama --model qwen... "Explain this code"
```

Then:

```bash
alkem explain ./src/foo.py
```

This validates:

```text
Client → Core → Gateway → Provider
```

before introducing more infrastructure.

---

## Milestone 4 — Repository intelligence

Goal: make ALKEM aware of a codebase.

Capabilities:

- repository scanning;
- file/symbol selection;
- contextual questions;
- code explanation;
- small generated modifications.

Avoid embeddings initially if deterministic file selection is sufficient.

---

## Milestone 5 — Retrieval / Knowledge

Goal: augment models with external material.

First vertical slice:

```text
PDF/document
→ extraction
→ chunks
→ embeddings
→ retrieval
→ model answer with context
```

Validate locally where practical.

---

## Milestone 6 — Sessions & Memory

Implement:

- conversation sessions;
- persisted history;
- context selection;
- side-chat branches.

Only after real usage exists, introduce richer memory concepts.

---

## Milestone 7 — Tool execution

Implement controlled tools such as:

- repository read;
- symbol lookup;
- test execution;
- potentially controlled patch generation/application.

Introduce explicit permissions and safety boundaries.

---

## Milestone 8 — VS Code extension

Build the first rich client around already validated ALKEM capabilities.

Initial scope:

- chat panel;
- selected-code context;
- explain;
- propose change;
- side-chat.

Do not put orchestration logic in the extension.

---

# 17. Explicit non-goals for the first milestones

Do NOT initially build:

- autonomous multi-agent systems;
- generic agent framework;
- complex workflow DSL;
- distributed vector database;
- Kubernetes infrastructure;
- fine-tuning pipeline;
- automatic model benchmarking system;
- intelligent cost optimization;
- dozens of provider integrations;
- full IDE replacement;
- generic memory framework.

These may be revisited when concrete product requirements justify them.

